{
  "dom_id": "step-q134105",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5768d8f90d3dd754471a69d25582eca6cdb2f4993b9b22020dc9f2038aa61954.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above summarizes data collected by a Midwestern high school showing the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the class size. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one class reported a total of $6$ absences in the month.\n- Two classes have a total of $20$ students each.\n- Only one class has more than $24$ students.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two points whose vertical coordinate is equal to $6,$ namely, $(16,6)$ and $(20,6).$ This means that two of the classes each reported a total of 6 absences in the month.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/a62b1d5a63764b38013fdbdba9ba85a4495cd996a2d9f975dbe3d7eb89166234.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $20,$ namely, $(20,6).$ This means that only one of the classes has a total of  $20$ students.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/3c41f2e111ef141511ec4f2faa655ddcea8f2b7e0b73bd37f0b1e142d5d60f14.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. From the scatter plot, only one class has more than $24$ students. This class is represented by the point to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/adcba37370fdac69b152a8d18ef710d5f665d9a3252376ea312808be7d08a407.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
